// Readme explaination 
Problem Statement

Given an integer n, return true if it is a power of two. Otherwise, return false.

A number is a power of two if it can be expressed as (2^x), where x is a non-negative integer.

Approach: Repeated Division

If n <= 0, return false, because powers of two are positive.

While n is divisible by 2, divide it by 2.

If the final value is 1, return true; otherwise, return false.



class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfTwo(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }

        while (n % 2 == 0) {
            n = n / 2;
        }

        return n == 1;
    }
}
